1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
This video introduces the new feature of Closet.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
This season, we have released a series of new features

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
that make it easy for users to check 3D clothing on Closet.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
One of the important updates is the 2D version of the viewfinder.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Just like in the Closet software,

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:27,000
users can check the 2D paper in the 3D file on Closet.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,000
On the left side, click on the shrink chart of the 2D window

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,000
to display the 2D paper.

9
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Just like Closet,

10
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,000
users can change the display options through the 2D menu.

11
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,000
For example, we can display the kill line direction

12
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,000
and check if all the kill line directions are correctly set.

13
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,000
In addition,

14
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,000
we can add views directly in the 2D viewfinder

15
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,000
to add comments or record any necessary modifications.

16
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:02,000
If you do not need to use the 2D viewfinder,

17
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,000
you can use this option.

18
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Click on the settings button under the company layer.

19
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,000
In the general settings, you can see that

20
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,000
the 2D version of the viewfinder is activated.

21
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Then click to stop it.

22
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,000
After you click on it,

23
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:22,000
you can notice the shrink chart of the 2D version of the viewfinder.

24
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,000
In the 3D clothing viewfinder, you cannot see

25
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:30,000
the shrink chart of the 2D version of the viewfinder.

26
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Even if you are an inexperienced user,

27
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:40,000
you can check the 2D version of the viewfinder online.

28
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:43,000
We also released a 3D quality check tool

29
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:47,000
for automatically detecting the attribute settings of 3D clothing.

30
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,000
To use this function,

31
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,000
we must activate it first.

32
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Under the company file layer,

33
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,000
click on the settings button.

34
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Find the content in the navigation bar.

35
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Select 3D quality check.

36
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:05,000
It is currently in the state of active.

37
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Click to activate it.

38
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:12,000
To check the quality of the 3D file created in the hole,

39
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,000
you can set the standard according to the specific requirements.

40
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:21,000
For example, we can set the particle diameter to 3-5.

41
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Find here and enter 3-5.

42
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:26,000
And set the clothing to close the hardening function.

43
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:30,000
After the setting is complete,

44
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:33,000
click on the application about how to configure the check chart

45
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,000
and more detailed information to check the results.

46
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,000
You can click on the PDF guide in the upper right corner.

47
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,000
You can access the PDF guide here

48
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,000
to learn more details.

49
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,000
After setting the quality check standard,

50
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:49,000
upload the 3D clothing to be quality checked.

51
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:52,000
On the left side of the content page, you can see the QC mark.

52
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Click on it.

53
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Click on the QC mark in the content page.

54
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,000
If the property is in line with the standard,

55
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,000
it will be marked as green.

56
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:05,000
If not, it will be marked as red.

57
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,000
You can click on the check mark.

58
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:12,000
To check in detail which specific parts of the file are not in line with the standard.

59
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,000
In this way,

60
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:16,000
you can check the quality of the 3D clothing in the close set.

61
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:20,000
You can simplify the workflow more efficiently.

62
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Next, let's look at the 3D clothing.

63
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Next, let's look at the QC mark.

64
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:28,000
QC managers can check the quality of the 3D clothing

65
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,000
in a more efficient way than before.

66
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:35,000
QC managers can activate the QC mark in advance.

67
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,000
On the left side of the control panel,

68
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:41,000
click on the QC setting.

69
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Click on the QC mark.

70
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,000
After clicking on this option,

71
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,000
when the existing users in the working area

72
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,000
invite new users to enter the working area,

73
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:51,000
they must first obtain the approval of the QC manager,

74
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:53,000
in order to complete the process.

75
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,000
For example,

76
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:57,000
when the existing users invite other users as observers

77
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,000
to enter the working area,

78
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:05,000
the required users will be marked as pre-checked.

79
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:06,000
In this process,

80
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,000
QC managers will receive email notifications

81
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,000
and check accordingly.

82
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,000
To continue to check,

83
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,000
QC managers can click on the user history record

84
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:18,000
on the control panel on the left side.

85
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Select the full line check option,

86
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,000
and then click on the QC mark.

87
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,000
Under the pre-checked users,

88
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:26,000
QC managers can choose to agree or reject users.

89
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,000
By using this function,

90
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:31,000
QC managers can fully master the invitation details in the group,

91
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,000
to achieve higher security

92
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:36,000
and better control of subscription costs.

